# November 19, 2026: Orleans County, Vermont, with Island Pond just over the line in Essex County (region vtn,
# Northern Vermont & Champlain Valley), first pass. Drawn at random by tools/choose.py, which named Brownington Village.
# Brownington's Old Stone House museum village, the factory ruins of Barton's Brick Kingdom and the CCC bathhouse on
# Crystal Lake, Newport's courthouse row and library, the Haskell library and opera house on the Canadian border, Irasburg's
# town hall, the Holland and Greensboro Bend survivors, East Charleston's store, the Orne bridge, the Clyde River dam and
# the site of Runaway Pond (1810).
# Facts come from Wikipedia articles read through tools/wiki_raw.py (most summarise the National Register form), HMdb
# marker texts, the Vermont Historical Society's Essex and Orleans museum directory, and the managing bodies' own pages
# read through tools/page.py, as linked on each place.
